The  file  describes  the various attributes of login classes.  A
login class determines what styles of authentication  are  avail‐
able  as  well  as session resource limits and environment setup.
While designed primarily for the program,  it  is  also  used  by
other  programs,  e.g.,  which need to set up a user environment.
The class to be used is normally determined by the field  in  the
password  file  (see The class is used to look up a corresponding
entry in the file.  A special class called will be  used  (if  it
exists) if the field in the password file is empty.  Refer to for
a  description  of  the file layout.  An example entry is: class‐
name|Description       entry:\                :capability=value:\
        :booleancapability:\                  ...          :last‐
capability=value: All entries in the file are either  boolean  or
use  a  ‘=’ to separate the capability from the value.  The types
are described after the capability table.

